WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.507
Jingzhang 100: the AI Artery. A centennial railway narrative meets agent-era infrastructure, in an agent-authored urban design proposal.

2
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:22.896
The overall structure: one heritage corridor as the spine, three innovation cores, multiple scenario nodes, and a blue-green mobility loop.

3
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:34.106
Within the eleven point four square kilometer design area, land use, buildings, roads, green space and public space are structured layers with recomputable metrics.

4
00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:47.259
Three key areas: Zhongzhiyuan Park for full-stack AI innovation; the Beijing AI Origin Community linking campuses and open source; Dazhongsi for agent-native business.

5
00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:57.751
The blue-green network: the heritage corridor, Qinghe and Xiaoyue riverfronts, and pocket parks, stitching five-minute living circles.

6
00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:12.143
The visitor journey: arrival, walking, interaction, staying, and participation. Every AI touchpoint keeps human takeover, non-digital channels, and a public veto button.

7
00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:24.688
All judgments are conceptual suggestions on provisional boundaries, recalculated once official geometry is released. Explore the full evidence chain in the offline visual page.
